#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0252-B expect=violation domain=ADSL
#note "Five columns, five template families: AOCC01FL matches ^AOCC(0[1-9]|[1-9]\d)FL$, TRTEM1FL matches ^TRTEM[1-9]FL$, TREM01FL matches ^TREM(0[1-9]|[1-9]\d)FL$, ACAT1 matches ^ACAT([1-9]|[1-9][0-9])$ and LBORG1 matches ^.+ORG[1-9]$. Since Fix #270 (ruling M2-D3) each family is its own varname() regex disjunct evaluated per variable, so the expander's five-capture-group cross-join is GONE and each column fires INDEPENDENTLY -> FIVE violations (pre-#270 the cross-join required all five groups to match at once and emitted ONE dataset-level violation; the owner ruled the independent reading correct, M2-D3 sub-decision 2). LBORG1 is now pinned too: the *ORGw arm - the one Check arm the old Output_Variables list missed (finding AD0252-B-F2, retired by Output_Variables -> [variable_name]) - goes live for the first time."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
#expectViolationCount 5
#expectViolationAt variable_name=AOCC01FL
#expectViolationAt variable_name=TRTEM1FL
#expectViolationAt variable_name=TREM01FL
#expectViolationAt variable_name=ACAT1
#expectViolationAt variable_name=LBORG1
dataset ADSL structure=ADSL
col STUDYID  type=Char
col USUBJID  type=Char
col AOCC01FL type=Char
col TRTEM1FL type=Char
col TREM01FL type=Char
col ACAT1    type=Char
col LBORG1   type=Char
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | Y | Y | Y | CAT1 | ORGA
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1023 | Y | Y | Y | CAT1 | ORGA
